WHAT CHANGED (audit class before: LOGIC-ONLY — the checkpoint crate's
DeltaJournal (baseline + whole-file deltas + cursors, pure restore) and
epoch-fenced CheckpointStore had unit tests and ZERO production callers)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
- domain: WorktreeCheckpointed run event (strictly increasing epoch +
  serialized DeltaJournal, emitter-bounded to 256 KiB; beyond that git
  remains the full-fidelity worktree record).
- scheduler: WorktreeJournalWriter rides the run plane — every
  successful change.apply records the PRE-EDIT bytes as the path's
  baseline (first touch wins) and the post-edit content as a delta,
  then persists one durable checkpoint event through the M4.4
  lease-fenced append path. Epoch fencing is crate-enforced: strictly
  increasing writes only; stale writes rejected and audited, never
  applied.
- restore stays pure in the crate (DeltaJournal::restore).

